":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1e176c91f0eddbdb6eef48a070b8ac73947d5e8c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1e176c91f0eddbdb6eef48a070b8ac73947d5e8c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 3:46PM MDT until October 26 at 9:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is ongoing\n\n* WHERE...Western Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...\nSouthern San Juan County in southeastern Utah...\n\n* WHEN...Until 900 AM MDT Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along San Juan River is occurring. Low-water\ncrossing are inundated with water and may not be passable. The\nriver is running fast and high. Do not attempt to cross.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 342 PM MDT, The San Juan River is forecast to crest tonight\naround midnight between Bluff and Mexican Hat. A second rise and\nhigher crest is forecast along the San Juan River, peaking at\nMexican Hat Sunday Monday.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nSan Juan River\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMexican Hat, Tselakai Dezza, Bluff, Halchita, Montezuma Creek and\nAneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-26T09:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3a13c08d00e9f0eaecf417945ed4320e5cfecd7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3a13c08d00e9f0eaecf417945ed4320e5cfecd7.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-24T17:22:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 241722 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service G